  "title": "Chapter 17 – Nursing Research & Statistics",
  "order": 17,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "06kk6mn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nursing research provides a scientific foundation for evidence-based practice and improved patient outcomes.",
        "The research process systematically moves from problem identification to data collection, analysis, and interpretation.",
        "Sampling techniques are classified into probability (random) and non-probability methods.",
        "Data analysis relies on measures of central tendency (Mean, Median, Mode) and measures of dispersion (Range, Variance, Standard Deviation).",
        "Effective presentation of data uses tables, graphs, and charts to communicate statistical findings clearly."
      ],
      "id": "btri5nr"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
