      "content": "Presentation of Data"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Median is the preferred measure of central tendency for highly skewed distributions, whereas Mean is sensitive to extreme values.",
        "Standard Deviation is the most stable and widely used measure of variability/dispersion in inferential statistics.",
        "Simple Random Sampling ensures every element in the target population has an equal, non-zero chance of selection.",
        "Phenomenology explores lived human experiences (Qualitative), whereas Experimental studies test cause-and-effect relationships (Quantitative)."
      ],
      "id": "4gsp78l"
    },
